	<description>NSLS-II BMM (6-BM) beamline model, improved from bmm_final.xml.

STARTUP CONFIGURATION: documented photon delivery mode C
(focused at the XAS sample, 6 to 8 keV, both mirrors in the beam,
M3 on the bare-Si stripe), tuned at the Fe K edge, 7112 eV.
Per the manual mode table: A focused above 8 keV (M2 only); B focused below
6 keV (unavailable at the real beamline); C focused 6 to 8 keV; D unfocused
above 8 keV (M3 only, Rh/Pt); E unfocused 6 to 8 keV; F unfocused below
6 keV; XRD focused at the goniometer above 8 keV. At high energy only ONE of
M2/M3 is in the beam; at low energy the HRM or both. Mode C is the natural
startup here because both mirrors are in the flow: rays that fly over a
retracted optic carry state=3 and are invisible to screens until the next
optic re-intersects them, so a mode with the LAST mirror (M3) retracted
(A, XRD) cannot produce sample-camera images unless M3 is removed from the
flow. Mode changes (a change_mode analogue) move: M2 center z (+50 mm = out),
M2 R (bender), M3 center z / pitch (sign flips to -0.0035 when leveling the
rising 7 mrad beam in D/E/F), M3 material (rhpt01 vs si01 stripe), DCM bragg
and cryst2perpTransl, and the downstream shutter/slit/screen heights.
Per-mode angles CONFIRMED from the beamline lookup table Modes.xlsx
(mirrors sheet): mode A: M2 3.5 mrad, M3 parked out of beam (jacks -1.5
uniform); mode B: M3 5.0 mrad, Si; mode C: M2 3.5 mrad AND M3 3.5 mrad, Si
stripe (m3 lateral -8); mode D: M3 3.5 mrad, Rh/Pt (lateral +8); mode E:
M3 3.5 mrad, Si; mode F: M3 5.0 mrad, Si; XRD: M2 only. M2 retracts in
D/E/F by moving all three jacks to +6 mm (upward). M2 bender: 216900 steps
in all XAS-focus modes vs 107240 for XRD focus (constrains the XRD-mode R).
M2 to M3 = 1908 mm (Modes.xlsx, matches this model exactly).

Sources for parameter values:
- BMM beamline manual, https://nsls2.github.io/bmm-beamline-manual/ (layout, mirror
  coatings Rh 5 nm on Pt 30 nm, M1 paraboloid at 13 m, DM2 slits typical 18 x 1.3 mm,
  M3 stripes: bare Si below 8 keV, Rh/Pt above; pitch 3.5 mrad)
- Musardo et al., NIM-A 1059 (2024) 169008 (3PW: B peak 1.1427 T, Ec 6.8 keV)
- NSLS2/bmm-profile-collection geometry constants (DCM offset 30 mm, M2 to M3
  distance 1905 mm, M2 pitch 3.5 mrad, XAFS table 11.5 to 12.7 m from M2)
- Modes.xlsx (beamline lookup table, provided by staff): front-end slits
  FE_MASK blades outboard +3.8 / inboard -4.2 / top +0.55 / bottom -0.55
  (8.0 x 1.1 mm); DM3 end-station slits +-4.0 x +-0.5 mm (added as DM3_Slits;
  its longitudinal position within DM3, y=39500 = M3+9119, is approximate);
  per-mode mirror angles and jack/bender positions as listed above; DCM
  calibration: Si(111) d = 3.1356369 A, bragg offset 16.054 deg (xrt uses its
  own Si d-spacing 3.135458 A, a 6e-5 relative difference, about 0.4 eV at
  the Fe K edge - relevant only for absolute energy calibration).
Tuned (not documented): M2 sagittal radius r = 82.789 mm and meridional
R = 6.758e6 mm chosen to place both foci at the XAS sample with pitch 3.5 mrad;
mirror slope errors (FE_M1, FE_M2, rms=4.5, i.e. about 6 urad tangential each)
fitted to the documented focused spot of about 300 x 250 um FWHM - this is an
EFFECTIVE value lumping polish error with vibration/thermal blur; real
metrology would likely show below 2 urad with the remainder from other
sources.

This model contains NO automatic adjustments: all angles and translations are
static motor-like values. Acquisition logic must coordinate them itself.
DCM motor formulas (Si 111, d = 3.135458 A, hc = 12398.42 eV A):
  bragg = arcsin(hc / (2 d E)) - dtheta_refraction(E) + 0.00700 rad
          (the 0.00700 rad term is the upward beam inclination after M1)
  cryst2perpTransl = 30 / (2 cos(bragg)) mm   (maintains the 30 mm fixed exit)
  cryst2longTransl : free motor; footprint walks along crystal 2 with angle.
The source samples photon energies only within eMin..eMax; widen or slide this
band (simulation-side, not hardware) to cover any energy scan.
Vertical geometry: beam rises at 7.000 mrad after M1, DCM adds +30 mm offset,
M2 (bounce-down 3.5 mrad) levels the beam, M3 (bounce-down 3.5 mrad) sends it
down at 7.0 mrad to the XAS and XRD sample positions.
Screens expose with withHistogram=True: after each trace, every screen holds a
flux-weighted image (attribute .image) on its limPhysX/limPhysY/histShape grid;
post-process with bmm_camera_view.py (PSF, exposure, 8-bit) to emulate cameras.</description>
